{
 "encounter_id": "00658",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hi. Um, thanks for seeing me. I'm still getting this ache in my lower tummy, even after the treatment, and I wasn't sure if that's normal."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "No, you did the right thing coming back. Remind me, how long since we started the treatment? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two weeks. I've nearly finished the course. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And the ache, where exactly?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Low down, in the middle and a bit on the right. A dull ache, mostly. It's better than it was, but it's not gone."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good, that's an improvement. Have you had any fever since the first week?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. The fever went after about three days. Nothing since."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any discharge?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Not now, no. That's stopped."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And any burning when you pass urine?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, none of that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's check what you're taking, to make sure it all matches."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Doxycycline, 100 mg twice a day, and metronidazole, 400 mg twice a day. And ibuprofen, 400 mg when it's really bad."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Any trouble with the tablets, sickness, upset stomach? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bit queasy with the metronidazole, but I take it with food and that helps. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Right. Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No allergies that I know of."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And is there anything on your record I should be aware of?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Endometriosis, diagnosed three years ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And do you smoke?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I smoke about five a day, I've been meaning to cut down."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "We can talk about that another time. Your temperature and pulse, please. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Temperature 36.8, pulse 76.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's good, isn't it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Very good. No fever, nothing worrying there. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "So what's the ache, if the infection's going? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It could be the last of the inflammation settling, but I can't rule out an ovarian cyst, especially with your history of endometriosis."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh. Is that serious? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Usually not. Many cysts are harmless and settle by themselves. But I'd like to keep an eye on it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What should I do? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Finish both courses, even if you feel better, and take the ibuprofen with food only when you need it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. And what if the ache doesn't go? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If it's still there in two weeks, I'll arrange a pelvic ultrasound."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And I'd like to see you again in two weeks anyway, either way."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Two weeks. Okay. Thank you. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Take care. Come back sooner if the pain suddenly gets worse or you get a temperature."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. ~"
  }
 ],
